          "message": {
            "text": "panic-unwrap: the user-supplied path segment is parsed with .unwrap(). Any request like GET /users/abc (or /users/ with trailing content that is not a u64) panics the handler thread; combined with main.rs dropping the handler Result, this silently kills connections and can take down the service. Use a match / .map_err and return HTTP 400 instead."
          },
          "ruleId": "panic-unwrap"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/svc-api/src/handlers.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 36,
                  "startLine": 36
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "panic-unwrap: POST /orders parses the raw request body with serde_json::from_str(...).unwrap(). Any malformed/non-JSON body (trivially reachable from the network, and note read_to_string here may return a truncated body since read_request already consumed part of the stream) panics. Return 400 Bad Request on Err instead. (Also note serde_json is not declared in crates/svc-api/Cargo.toml, so this file cannot currently compile.)"
          },
          "ruleId": "panic-unwrap"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
