                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "panic-unwrap (minor): first_id unwraps split(',').next(). For a str input this iterator always yields at least one element, so it cannot actually panic at runtime — but the unwrap is misleading since the surrounding parse already returns Option via `?`; the idiomatic form is raw.split(',').next().unwrap_or_default() or a direct match/and_then. Note: models.rs is not declared with `mod models;` in crates/svc-core/src/lib.rs, so this code is currently dead/unreachable."
          },
          "ruleId": "panic-unwrap"
        },
