          "message": {
            "text": "swallowed-error: the io::Result of handle_connection is discarded with `let _ =`, so every failed read/parse/response write is invisible — clients hang or get truncated responses and there is no log to diagnose it. At minimum log the error (e.g. `if let Err(e) = ... { eprintln!(\"handler error: {e}\") }`), ideally per-connection tracing, and consider a thread/task per connection."
          },
          "ruleId": "swallowed-error"
        },
